MCP: 
MCPs follow a client-server architecture, agents use the MCP client to interact with an MCP server, so usually MCP clients are embedded within coding agents in IDEs like Cursor, Claude Code.
MCP server have 3 components: Resources for information, Tools for actions, and Prompts for reusable instructions
MCP client have 3 components: 
roots: safe folders willing to expose to the server.
sampling: allows servers to request LLM responses from clients. $ uv run python sampling_client.py
          the client has control over the model selection, token limits, etc.  
elicitation: allows servers to request user input from clients. $ uv run python elicitation_client.py

