Build a MCP server:
1. import the FastMCP library and initialise a MCP server from it
2. define tools, resources and prompts
3. run the server and specify a transport protocol, either Standand IO or HTTP


Setting up a MCP project:
1. cd /home/project
2. uv init project-name             //creates a proper Python project with pyproject.toml
3. cd project-name
4. uv add "mcp[cli]==1.2,<2"        //Add MCP dependencies with CLI tools: mcp[cli] includes both MCP SDK and development tools (MCP Inspector)


Kubernetes MCP Server: an MCP server that provides Kubernetes resources and operational capabilities to AI agents through the MCP protocol.


